{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>וילדו.</b> It returns to the wife of Abimelech and his maidservants, not to Abimelech. And likewise \"וישם דמי מלחמה בשלום\" (1 Kings 2:5), \"בעמוד ענן ידבר אליהם\" (Psalms 99:7), \"אלה בני עדה\" (Genesis 36:16), \"אשר עבדתי אותך בהן\" (Genesis 30:26), \"אבי אברהם ואבי נחור ויעבדו\" (Joshua 24:2). Do you not see that it is explicit in the second verse: \"כי עצר עצר ד' בעד כל רחם לבית אבימלך\" — and he did not mention Abimelech. And I have lengthened thus far on account of commentators who used to say that he was prevented from going outside,"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The initial lemma 'וילדו' (v. 17, 'and they bore [children]') does not match any standard Genesis 20:17 text; retained as in the source. The fragmentary closing clause about Abimelech being 'prevented from going outside' breaks off without completing the thought, translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:18.162087397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}